<h1 style="font-size:2rem;font-weight:800;">A/B Testing Links</h1>
<p>Test multiple landing pages against each other to find the highest-converting version.</p>

<h2>Setting Up an A/B Test</h2>
<ol><li>Create a link and select <strong>A/B Test</strong> as the redirect mode</li><li>Add two or more <strong>destination URLs</strong></li><li>Set the <strong>traffic weight</strong> for each variant (e.g., 50/50)</li><li>Optionally set an <strong>end date</strong> for the test</li><li>Create the link and share it</li></ol>

<h2>Analyzing Results</h2>
<p>On the link detail page, you'll see:</p>
<ul><li>Click count per variant</li><li>Conversion rate per variant (if tracking events)</li><li>Traffic distribution over time</li></ul>

<h2>Best Practices</h2>
<ul><li>Test one variable at a time (headline, image, CTA)</li><li>Run tests for at least 7 days for statistical significance</li><li>Use 50/50 splits for fair comparison</li><li>Track conversions, not just clicks</li></ul>

<h2>Plan Requirement</h2>
<p>A/B Testing is available on the <strong>Business plan</strong> and above.</p>
